\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces E-R4' on untouched inputs (4 breaking directions $\times $ $8$ optimiser seeds: $8$ units at $\eta {=}0$, $32$ at $\eta {>}0$), next to the same unit subset on development rows. The untouched data reproduce the WP-REPAIR-2 reading: the repaired arm beats the original architecture, the gate-count-matched duplicate control is \emph  {not} beaten at $\eta {=}0$, and enforcing invariance costs $0.046$ of risk at $\eta {=}1$. Magnitudes differ slightly from Table~\ref {tab:rep2} because this is a subset of directions and seeds.}}{13}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
